.TH geectl-remote-search-packages 1  "geectl-remote-search-packages 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-search\-packages \- Search packages by name. Substring matches on name, title, and description by default; `\-\-exact` keeps only exact\-name matches (the filter runs client\-side). With `\-\-devel\-project`, only packages developed in that project; without a term, every package the devel project develops
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote search\-packages\fR [\fB\-\-exact\fR] [\fB\-\-devel\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITERM\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search packages by name. Substring matches on name, title, and description by default; `\-\-exact` keeps only exact\-name matches (the filter runs client\-side). With `\-\-devel\-project`, only packages developed in that project; without a term, every package the devel project develops
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-exact\fR
Only show packages whose name is exactly the term
.TP
\fB\-\-devel\-project\fR \fI<DEVEL_PROJECT>\fR
Only show packages developed in this project
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fITERM\fR]
The search term; required unless `\-\-devel\-project` is given
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
